DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T111500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T143000
SUMMARY:Worlds Edge Tr\; a Saunter
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nLocated in the western-most backside of Chi
 mney Rock St Pk – above the Edneyville orchards. With vast views of the 
 NC Piedmont. On a clear day\, you can see Kings Mtn (80 mi/Charlotte)\nRem
 ember - hikes led by ‘the Curmudgeon’ tend to have pleasant surprises.
 \nI will be carrying the ‘Ent-Ward’ that gives us permission to pass t
 hru the forest.\n**Difficulty:** “off-trail conditions”. Some very cha
 llenging footing along **unfenced** cliff edge\; plus 'cliff edge' overloo
 ks. A few steep challenging footing sections. **Middle ¼ mile will be ‘
 off-trail’ thru brush.**\nBring cutting snips and folding handsaws if yo
 u have them.\nUp to 8 (only) of you are welcome to join me.\n**IF YOU HAVE
  AN ORANGE VEST\; WEAR IT. HUNTING SEASON HAS STARTED. \;-) THEY ARE INEXP
 ENSIVE AT WALMART....**\nWe are the Sloth Hike Team of WNC: “We will get
  there when we get there.” We dare to go where the ‘real’ hike group
 s don’t ***!!***\n**https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TQ8H4EK2vt4**\nDetai
 ls:\nI am going to **scout\, trim and assess** the cliff edge of the World
 ’s Edge Tr near Edneyville\;\nLength: 2.0 miles round-trip\; accum ascen
 t: 300 feet\, most on the return on rocky forest rd. Pace: **1.5mph.**\nDr
 ive time: 20 min 1-way\nGoogle maps= “Ottanola Gap”\nCarpool contribut
 ions appreciated. $3.00 suggested\nApprx return time: 2:30pm\n**Dogs: ONLY
  well-trained dogs because of the unfenced cliff edge. And leashes will ta
 ngle in the brush.**\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\
 nI currently have 2.5 driver. (limit 9)\nWeather Check: Edneyville\, NC\nI
 ncessant prattlers will be assumed to be having an affair.\n**Optional**: 
 after the hike\, Dine at Kin’s Chinese Kitchen. 2560 Chimney Rock Rd\nWe
  suggest masks and open windows while carpooling. Only you know your own h
 ealth status so judge accordingly if an event may endanger your health or 
 the health of others.\nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringi
 ng your muddy shoes into the driver's car at the end of the hike.\nAll hik
 es are at your own risk. You are responsible for your OWN safety and adequ
 ate equipment.\nWaiver: There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor ac
 tivity. Each participant\, by signing up to attend this event\, agrees to 
 release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners\, 
 Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or personal
  loss which might occur while participating in this activity or while trav
 eling in any vehicle during this trip. **Each participant further agrees t
 o abide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\, to follow instruc
 tions of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally separated from th
 e group.** The leader(s) also has the right to use any images collected on
  this trip for recording on website photo collections.\ngordie's contact: 
 CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 ( text o
 nly)\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/https-www-meetup-com-hendo-fun-friend
 s/events/317267902/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261103T093504Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261103T093504Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
