BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Avl Digital Nomads": "https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/317276199/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_avl_digital_nomads
X-SOURCE:AVL Digital Nomads
UID:event_317276199@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261114T061159Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T200000
SUMMARY:The Leadership Lounge: The Three Pillars
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\nYou want to do your best work every time. 
 It's important to you\, and you care about how you show up and what your t
 eam thinks of you.\nBeing present for ourselves is a significant challenge
  that often creates a gap. This gap represents the difference between the 
 way we aspire to live and how we actually live. We choose to bridge this g
 ap because it is the right thing to do.\n\nIntroducing a great way for new
  nomads to connect and discover important key takeaways for their lives. A
 s a new Asheville Digital Nomad\, where do you go if you don’t know many
  people?\n\nYou will participate in a discussion\, yes! YOU\, the audience
 \, will be a part of a wonderful panel discussion. Whether you are a veter
 an or a newbie\, come to **The Leadership Lounge**. You will get something
  out of this event and gain new insights to improve your outlook on how we
 ll you are settling into Asheville and Western North Carolina.\n\n**The Le
 adership Lounge** presents a fabulous evening: **The Three Pillars.** This
  special occasion will introduce you to new actions to manage burnout and 
 physiological changes\, combining practicality with an intuitive desire fo
 r more fun.\n**Pillar I - Somatic Sovereignty**: Lindsay Coward\n**Pillar 
 II - Self-Leadership**: Stacy Antos\n**Pillar III - The Sovereign Career**
 : Jane Carter\n\n***Special discount* on 'ADN'-engraved Pirani cups! 5th-a
 nniversary custom ADN Pirani cups!**\n**Available in 16 oz\, 26 oz\, and 3
 2 oz for $15\, $20\, and $25.**\n\nEveryone! Whether you're leading in for
 -profit\, non-profit\, academia\, community organizations\, or entrepreneu
 rship – or simply curious about leadership – you're welcome to join us
 .\n\n* Free Parking\n* Beverages: Alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages\n\
 nCome join us. Meet new people. Take away some next steps.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/317276199/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261103T221928Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261103T221928Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Shutupandwriteasheville": "https://www.meetup.com/shutupandwriteasheville/events/317181373/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_shutupandwriteasheville
X-SOURCE:Shut Up & Write Western NC
UID:event_317181373@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261114T061224Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T193000
SUMMARY:Shut Up & Write!® - Downtown
DESCRIPTION:Shut Up & Write!® Western North Carolina\n***\\*\\*\\*Please 
 note: event listings are moving to the Shut Up & Write! website and this M
 eetup page will be closed in a few weeks. You will find our Tuesday night 
 events here: [https://www.shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00](https://www
 .shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00)\\*\\*\\****\n\n**Here's how it works
 .** Show up at or before 6:00. At 6:00\, we do some quick introductions. A
 fterward\, for a full 60 minutes (I'll set a timer!) we are heads-down wri
 ting. Writing what? A novel? You bet. Some poetry? Sure. Song lyrics? Your
  resume? That report you need to get to your boss before 8 AM or you'll *n
 eed* *to write* that resume? All of the above and more. Just shut up and w
 rite.\n\nSurrounding ourselves with other writers who are busy putting wor
 ds onto page (physical or virtual) keeps us all accountable and focused.\n
 \nWhen the timer goes off\, we'll check-in with each other and see how it 
 went. Afterward\, feel free to stay to chat and get to know your fellow wr
 iters\, or keep writing\, or take off.\n\nSocializing is optional and will
  happen after (or briefly before) the focused writing. This is a safe spac
 e to work on your craft. No one will read or critique your writing.\n\nFor
  more information about our events\, visit [https://shutupwrite.com](https
 ://shutupwrite.com).\n\n**What to Expect**\n\n* Roughly 15 minutes of intr
 oductions\n* 60 minutes of focused writing (somebody set a timer)!\n* Afte
 rward\, optional socializing\n\n**Being late is okay:** Just show up and g
 et settled\, then check in with the host after the session. (Look for the 
 person with the Shut Up & Write sign).\n\n**What Should I Bring?**\n\n* Wh
 atever you need to be able to write!\n* Earbuds/earplugs if you want to bl
 ock ambient noise.\n\n**Other Important Details:**\n\n***\\*\\*\\*Please n
 ote: Shut Up & Write event listings are moving to the Shut Up & Write! web
 site and this Meetup page will be closed. You will find our Tuesday night 
 events here: [https://www.shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00](https://www
 .shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00)\\*\\*\\****\n\nHOSTS: This is a mult
 i-host event\, so most of the time there will be a host present. If we are
  unlucky and no host can attend\, please find each other and self-organize
 . Pay attention to the event chat and comments to see who is available.\n\
 nWI-FI: Yes!\n\nPARKING: Street parking in metered spots is free after 6pm
 . Closest municipal garages ($2/hour) are Wall St. & Coxe Street/Sears All
 ey.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/shutupandwriteasheville/events/317181
 373/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261028T222510Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261028T222510Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
