BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Calendar Ics": "https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/without-shade-without-rest-film-screening-and-discussion"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_calendar_ics
X-SOURCE:Warren Wilson College
DTSTAMP:20261114T061230Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54303159122795
DTSTART:20261120T230000Z
DTEND:20261121T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us November 20\, at 6pm in Kittredge Theater for a screeni
 ng of the film Without Shade\, Without Rest. There will be light refreshme
 nts provided and a discussion of farm and food worker rights following the
  film. This screening is made possible by the Educating Character Initiati
 ve. \n\n \n\nWeCount! is a non-profit\, human rights organization that rep
 resents immigrant workers and families in South Florida\, including plant 
 nursery workers. WeCount!’s advocacy on extreme heat is the subject of t
 he new documentary\, Without Shade\, Without Rest by Six Eye Films and Wor
 king Films. This documentary tells the story of two organizations\, WeCoun
 t! and the Coalition of Immokalee Workers\, and our efforts to win heat pr
 otections for Florida’s outdoor workers. In the face of intense industry
  lobbying and aggressive state preemption\, the fight in Florida continues
 . Their work has helped put extreme heat in the national conversation and 
 inspired advocacy for workplace heat standards across the country. \n\n \n
 \nWhile “Without Shade\, Without Rest” is primarily focused on Florida
 \, we believe this film can be a helpful tool for workers\, advocates\, or
 ganizations\, and community members across the country and world\, who are
  similarly grappling with the growing and existential threat of climate ch
 ange and extreme heat. We hope the film helps shine a light on an urgent l
 abor and human rights issue and contributes to meaningful dialogue and con
 nections across our movements. In Asheville\, a new campaign Planting Just
 ice (Sembra Justicia) is being launched by WeCount! and local partners in 
 support of workers in the house plant industry who work locally with littl
 e labor protections. The food we eat and the plants we enjoy are nothing w
 ithout the workers who plant and nurture them.
GEO:35.613818;-82.438862
LOCATION:Kittredge Arts Center\, Kittredge Theater
SUMMARY:Without Shade\, Without Rest Film Screening and Discussion 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/without-shade-without-
 rest-film-screening-and-discussion
CATEGORIES:Lecture
CATEGORIES:Performance
CATEGORIES:Social
END:VEVENT
