BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Asheville Mountains To Sea Trail Hiking Club": "https://www.meetup.com/asheville-mountains-to-sea-trail-hiking-club/events/317341246/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_asheville_mountains_to_sea_trail_hiking_club
X-SOURCE:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club
UID:event_317341246@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261114T061155Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261123T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261123T110000
SUMMARY:Mountains-to-Sea Trail Highway 25 toward Bent Creek
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club 2.0\nThis is a fa
 irly easy hike\, and we go at a high average to low advanced speed\, which
  is roughly about 3.0 to 3.2 mph. There are no super long hills. It's pret
 ty undulating all the way.\n\nWell behaved dogs on leashes are welcome to 
 attend.\n\nWhen you arrive\, park at the gravel lot across from the trail 
 head. You'll see some people gathering by their cars. I've recently correc
 ted the PIN setting on the map\, so it should be correct. Here are some di
 rections to use too: When going south on Hendersonville Road\, go past Car
 olina Day School and turn right at the Blue Ridge Parkway exit. When you g
 et to the parkway turn RIGHT. You will see parking on the left and right s
 ide of the road. Park there.\n\nMountains-to-Sea-Trail hikes are designed 
 for fitness and community among people who are already reasonably fit. It'
 s not an endurance hike by any means\, but it is designed so we can get ou
 r hearts beating a bit while still being able to have a conversation and m
 eet new people.\nWhen you arrive\, we'll circle up and introduce ourselves
  briefly. There will be a person who is a sweep. This person is the person
  who walks last and makes sure no one gets lost.\n\nWe leave the parking s
 pot at 9:10. If someone needs a nature break\, we wait fo you\, but it's n
 ot a hike where we stop and take photos or frequent breaks. We basically k
 eep hiking until the 1/2 way mark\, then turn around after a short (approx
 imately 5 minute) break. Then we keep that same pace on the way back. If w
 e get on a trail right at 9:10\, we are normally finished around 10:50.\n\
 nThese are out and back hikes\, meaning that we hike in and turn around ha
 lf way to return back.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-mountains-to-sea-trail-hiki
 ng-club/events/317341246/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261108T161702Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261108T161702Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
