X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/motee-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261205T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261205T160000
DTSTAMP:20261112T162550Z
CREATED:20261019T191141Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261112T162550Z
UID:1778780020244-1796464800-1796486400@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Methods of Teaching Environmental Education Workshop\, NC EE Criteria I
DESCRIPTION:Methods of Teaching Environmental Education Workshop\, NC EE Criteria I\nwith Michelle Pearce \n4 hours of online self-guided online learning and \nIn-person Saturday\, December 5  |  10 am – 4 pm \nRegister Here!\nThe Methods of Teaching EE (MOTEE) workshop helps practitioners create inclusive and age-appropriate learning experiences\, gain group management skills\, practice teaching methods to promote inquiry\, and gain skills in designing objectives\, lessons\, and assessments for EE programs using NC Essential Standards as a foundation. This will be a hybrid workshop\, with 4 hours of online\, self-guided learning\, in addition to a 6 hour in person session. Participants will receive 10 hours of Criteria 1 credit toward their NC EE Certification. \nThis program will take place both in the classroom and outside following easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the part program time. \nMichelle Pearce has worked in Environmental Education since 2006. It was actually her first job right out of college\, and she fell in love with it! Michelle has been a seasonal staff\, Summer camp staff\, county parks staff\, a state employee\, an adjunct professor\, and now is currently serving as the Programming Lead for the Environmental Educators of North Carolina. She has a Bachelor’s degree in Biology with an emphasis in life science\, and a Masters of Arts in Education with an emphasis in Science Education. She currently resides in Candler with her son and her leopard gecko. \n●  Pre-registration is required for all classes unless otherwise detailed above. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! Or join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/motee-2026/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/20260618_105733.jpg
END:VEVENT
