BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/plant-ecology-dec-26/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261211T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261211T143000
DTSTAMP:20261020T173005Z
CREATED:20261020T173005Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261020T173005Z
UID:1778780020248-1796994000-1796999400@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Plant Ecology
DESCRIPTION:Plant Ecology\nwith Alexandra Holland \nFriday\, December 11  |  1 – 2:30pm \nBRN – Core  |  BREG – Elective \nRegister Here!\nPrerequisite: Beginning Botany \nIn this class we’ll explore a variety of ways plants interact with one another and with other organisms from fungi to insects.  We’ll examine how plants compete and cooperate to survive in their environment. \nAlexandra Holland has a passion for getting people excited about the natural world through classes\, hikes\, and photography.  She graduated from Duke University and earned her master’s degree in botany from the University of Texas at Austin.  While in Texas\, Alexandra managed the UTEX Culture Collection of Algae at UT Austin and volunteered with education programs at the Lady Bird Johnson Wildflower Center.  Upon moving to Asheville\, she began volunteering with the NC Arboretum’s youth education programs.  In 2008 she was in the first class of students to be certified as Blue Ridge Naturalists.   Alexandra teaches botany classes at the NC Arboretum and leads nature hikes in Western NC for groups of all ages. \n●  Pre-registration is required for all classes unless otherwise detailed above. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! Or join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/plant-ecology-dec-26/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education,BREG,BRN
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/ladybug_HeroWeb.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/naturalist-walk-and-talk-dec/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261211T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261211T150000
DTSTAMP:20261020T170148Z
CREATED:20261020T170148Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261020T170148Z
UID:1778780020246-1796994000-1797001200@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Naturalist Walk & Talk
DESCRIPTION:Naturalist Walk and Talk\nwith Shane Myers \nFriday\, December 11  |  1 – 3pm \nBRN – Elective \nRegister Here!\nWalk around the Arboretum with our staff naturalists and talk about what we see around us. We might see plants and animals\, and evidence of them going about their lives in our backyard. Topics will be based on what we see and experience and whatever questions that come up\, so every class has the potential to be quite different. \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \nShane Myers’ interest in nature began as a child with a love of dinosaurs. This quickly grew to include fossils\, insects\, and reptiles\, and learning from the notes his grandparents kept of the birds that came to their feeders in Toledo\, Ohio.  He has a Bachelors of Science in Wildlife Biology and did most of his undergraduate work on dragonflies and damselflies. He’s assisted in outreach and education for plant conservation groups\, Odonata Groups\, and various bird groups. Shane currently works for the Adult Education department at the NC Arboretum. \n●  Pre-registration is required for all classes unless otherwise detailed above. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! Or join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/naturalist-walk-and-talk-dec/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education,BRN
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/Winter_Watershed_webhero.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/winter-buds-bark-tree-id-dec-26/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261211T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261211T150000
DTSTAMP:20261020T174659Z
CREATED:20261020T171925Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261020T174659Z
UID:1778780020247-1796994000-1797001200@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Winter Buds & Bark Tree ID
DESCRIPTION:Winter Buds & Bark Tree ID\nwith Lauren Lampley \nFriday\, December 11  |  1 – 4pm \nBRN – Core |  BREG – Elective \nRegister Here!\nEver wondered how you can identify a tree without its leaves? All tree species have different patterns of bark and leaf/flower buds that can be used to identify them even in winter time. In this program\, we will look closely at the common trees around the NC Arboretum trails and point out specific characteristics of their buds and bark so you can identify them even without their leaves. \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \nLauren Lampley began her career at Grandfather Mountain Stewardship Foundation as a Park Naturalist which solidified Lauren’s interests in ecology and a passion for teaching others. She has led walks and hikes in a variety of subjects from Geology to Birding and especially enjoys learning and teaching about our local ecology. She currently works at the NC Arboretum as the Adult Education Coordinator managing all the programming hosted through the Adult Education Department. \n●  Pre-registration is required for all classes unless otherwise detailed above. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! Or join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/winter-buds-bark-tree-id-dec-26/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education,BRN
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Winter-bark-ID.jpg
END:VEVENT
